end;

questions.stem:
Suppose we define a static method totalEvenLoc() that returns the total for even-index items of an integer list as shown, on the right, below. What is the Big O running time of the method if lst is a LinkedList of size N?

public static int totalEvenLoc(List<Integer> lst) {
int sum = 0;
for(int i = 0; i < lst.size(); i += 2)
sum += lst.get(i);
return sum;
}

What will be the content of the queue (shown from queue front on the left to queue rear on the right), after the given sequence of operations shown below?

Queue q = new Queue();
q.enqueue(4);
q.enqueue(8);
if(q.peek() > 5)
q.dequeue();
q.enqueue(1);
q.enqueue(6);
q.dequeue();

